WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:06.170
<i>While Main is struggling to create colored 
inks, she finds out that Dirk has the Devouring.</i>

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:13.570
The high priest will take advantage
 of this if he finds out about it.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.740
Whether or not you are able 
to protect this infant

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.860
may greatly change your position 
and your surroundings.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.230
Always keep that in mind.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:23.930
Yes.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.330
The head priest can't be trusted!

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:29.540
He can be trusted.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.000
Fran, Delia.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:33.880
What's this all about?

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:39.550
Lady Main, is it true that Dirk 
is supposed to be adopted?

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:40.830
What?

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.860
Arno had brought over a 
message from the head priest

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:50.430
saying it would be difficult to find 
a noble to adopt Dirk after all.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:57.430
Why is the head priest talking 
about Dirk getting adopted?!

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:58.330
I...

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:02.170
Delia! How dare you treat 
Lady Main in such a manner!

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:03.820
Unhand her at once!

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:08.530
First Lady Main and her family, now Dirk and I.

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:12.790
Apparently, the head priest takes 
joy in ripping families apart!

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.600
That is not true!

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.940
The head priest has his own reasons.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.370
And what exactly would those reasons be?!

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:23.700
Delia.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:29.030
The one who asked the head 
priest to have Dirk adopted

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:30.840
is me.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:31.890
What?

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.500
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.010
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:17.960
<b>Chapter Thirty-Four
 Ominous Developments</b>

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:22.010
So you want to tear us apart, Lady Main?!

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:23.980
No.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:27.820
But all of us taking turns to take 
care of him is quite a burden.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:30.890
If someone wants to adopt Dirk,

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:34.890
I thought that maybe he 
could find some happiness.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:38.410
Even then! How could you decide 
this without telling me?!

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.180
It's just too cruel!

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:45.410
Currently, I'm grateful that you now all know 
about us trying to find someone to adopt Dirk.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:46.620
What?

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.120
Because I...

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:54.000
never thought you'd want to take 
care of Dirk so much, Delia.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.010
Lady Main...

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:02.110
The head priest has said that we probably 
will not be able to find anyone to adopt him.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:06.630
Even so, he is doing his 
best to find someone anyway.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.810
I see...

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:13.200
In Arno's message, apparently the head priest

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.110
asked us to continue looking 
after the child in the meantime.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:22.530
So Dirk and I won't be ripped apart, then?

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:28.170
Correct. I know how much you care for Dirk.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.530
And...

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:35.310
I personally know how it feels to not 
want to be away from your family.

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.280
Thank goodness.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:45.740
I don't want to be apart 
from Dirk, no matter what.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:49.670
He's the first time I've ever had... a family.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.690
Just a little more! You've got this, Dirk!

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:04.130
You're almost there, Dirk! 
You can do this! Come on!

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.620
You're amazing, Dirk!

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.790
I'd expect nothing less
from my little brother!

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.220
You're just wonderful.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:20.080
<i>Some time after, the doors were installed 
at Mister Benno's Italian restaurant,</i>

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:26.860
<i>and our fixing agent was completed.</i>

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:48.400
Who the hell are you?!

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:53.540
Josef! We've just been informed 
that Heidi's been captured!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.690
What?!

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:58.210
She came to steal our paint-making secrets.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:01.580
I wasn't trying to steal it...

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:04.460
I'm so sorry for the trouble 
my daydreaming wife caused...

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:08.670
If you're her husband, you need 
to keep better tabs on her.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:12.080
I'll do my best.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.100
Heidi, what were you doing there?

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:21.840
I was trying to find some inspiration 
and somehow ended up there.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:26.800
I wonder how we can make ink that the 
little miss will be satisfied with.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:29.280
That's seriously all you ever think about.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.200
Josef! Heidi!

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:35.200
We figured out how to make a fixing agent!

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.790
A fixing... agent?

00:06:42.390 --> 00:06:44.240
The color didn't change.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:45.090
And next...

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.360
It didn't turn black!

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:54.790
This is the first I've seen
it with my own eyes, too.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:01.550
Is something wrong, Heidi?

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:04.790
And it's over just like that.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:09.820
It's over before we ever found out 
what was causing that change.

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:15.580
I don't mind giving you a little money 
if you want to continue your research.

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:20.340
If we want to make these colors 
vibrant or create more colors,

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:22.380
basic research will be necessary.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:24.500
Miss, you're the best!

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.960
Miss, you're spoiling Heidi way too much.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:33.260
Well, to me, you're also Gutenbergs.

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:35.630
Guten... what now?

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:37.220
Now there's even more.

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:39.600
Gutenberg...

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.110
One of the most important people 
in the history of books.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:45.620
He's basically a god because of
the way he changed how they're created.

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:47.100
Currently, we have...

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:49.660
Johann, who created the metal letter types,

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:52.400
Mister Benno, who's making 
plant-based paper,

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:56.650
and Lutz, who sells books, as 
the Gutenbergs of this town.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:00.260
There's also Mister Ingo,
who makes our printing press,

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:02.390
and now you two, who make our inks.

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:06.120
I'm considering giving all of 
you the title of Gutenberg as well.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:11.340
Of course I don't mind investing in Gutenbergs, 
who will be vital in the creation of books.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:12.620
Right...

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:14.710
Did you hear that? We're Gutenbergs, Josef!

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:17.230
She'll invest in this!

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:19.690
I'll be allowed to do my research!

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:21.930
Yahoo!

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:25.000
Yeah, she's just like Main.

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:27.330
Heidi.

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:31.460
If you're unable to deliver the 
ink we order by the deadline,

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:34.830
I will be cutting off your 
funding. Just remember that.

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:35.570
Ack!

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:40.420
I guess it takes one to know one.
 Main has her figured out.

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:41.680
Takes one to know one?

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:48.670
Next, I'd like some wax paper.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:50.820
Even if we were going to make a substitute,

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:53.560
we'd need an iron and wax paper...

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:57.100
What are those, and where can you find them?

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:59.570
All in Lady Main's head.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:04.660
I'll do my best to try to figure 
out how to make all of that,

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:07.310
so I'll need you to take notes 
on your tablet when I do, Gil.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:10.680
I'll do my best, Lady Main!

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:16.200
Next, we went to the wax workshop to 
have Gil's tablet filled with wax.

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:18.520
Hello!

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:21.940
Hey, Gutenberg! Lady Main's here!

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:23.960
Stop calling me that.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:27.290
What brings you here today, Lady Main?

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:30.580
Well, I was hoping you'd be 
able to make Gil a stylus.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:35.370
And I was hoping you could 
make a toy for Kamil as well.

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:36.590
A toy?

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:40.980
I'm going to go straight home now.

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:44.660
What's that?

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:49.810
Isn't that...

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:50.790
We need to hurry!

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:54.390
Hey, where are we going?

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.660
This is a shortcut!

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:04.150
Apprentice Priestess,

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.600
I'm going to regroup with the knights 
to find out more information.

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:11.880
You are not to leave your 
house until I come back.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:12.530
Understood?

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:13.830
Yes.

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:16.000
Please watch after the apprentice priestess.

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:19.390
What in the world is going on?

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:21.730
Apparently, something 
happened at the east gate.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:22.920
The east gate?

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:26.350
I hope Dad is okay...

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:31.780
A noble from out of town tried to 
come in and caused a commotion.

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:37.590
They didn't know the policies at the gates 
had changed and had an unauthorized invitation.

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:42.710
Oh, "No nobles from other domains may 
enter without permission from the lord."

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:47.330
Yeah. Then they got mad at the gatekeeper 
for stopping their carriage.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.720
That's why we summoned the knights.

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:55.670
We have to summon the knights 
whenever nobles are involved.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:59.130
I guess everyone's put a lot 
of thought into all of this.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:04.220
If a dangerous noble tries to enter,

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:07.730
I will immediately call the 
knights and protect the gate.

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:11.680
So make sure you're aware 
of your surroundings, Main.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:15.350
What are you laughing about?

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:17.350
Oh, nothing.

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:25.920
<i>Dad's words made me so happy 
that I ended up smiling,</i>

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:28.790
<i>despite the situation we're in.</i>

00:11:47.510 --> 00:11:50.520
Stop getting in my way!

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:54.930
How dare all of you mock me?!

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:07.870
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:12:10.030 --> 00:12:13.960
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:16.710
Yours turn out so much cuter.

00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:20.650
Well, your seams definitely 
look better than mine.

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:25.280
You need to get better or sewing, or 
you'll never be able to get married.

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:30.230
That's fine! I plan to 
devote my life to books!

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:33.770
Lutz is here.

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:35.100
Lutz!

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:38.090
Johann finished a little something.

00:12:40.270 --> 00:12:41.730
The bell!

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.900
What are you going to do with that?

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:45.860
There we go.

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:49.530
Look, Kamil. It's done!

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:56.970
Just look at him! You're so precious, Kamil!

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:07.610
Kamil always seems to cry 
when he sees your face, Main.

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:09.060
Inconceivable.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:14.300
Big Sis Main!

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:18.610
I'm supposed to be the big sis 
adored by my little brother.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:21.180
I've got a long road ahead of me.

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:24.450
Main, when can you head to the cathedral?

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.030
No idea.

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:27.440
You've been home three days now, right?

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:30.090
I'm so bored, I don't know 
what to do with myself.

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:33.290
Then let's figure out what the 
next picture book should be.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.710
The next picture book?

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:37.680
I wonder...

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.790
About the trouble that 
happened at the east gate...

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:44.380
The one who had given an invitation 
to that noble from another domain

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:46.040
was the high priest.

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:50.060
They were given a stern 
warning from the knights.

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:55.600
And because the lord is away 
at a lords' gathering,

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:58.250
he won't be issuing any 
new permits at this time.

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:02.200
During this time, Main should be 
able to come to the cathedral.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:02.930
Yes, sir.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:06.840
But there is a possibility someone 
will try to forge the permits.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:09.970
Please let Main's father know of this matter.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:10.660
Yes, sir.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:18.960
<i>I was finally able to go to the cathedral after
 I'd been holed up at home for five days.</i>

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:22.750
That concludes Lord Ferdinand's message.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:23.810
Understood.

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:26.050
Okay, I'll be going now.

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:29.270
Be careful, Main.

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:45.820
It's really quiet. Is Dirk still asleep?

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:52.190
Upon the high priest's orders, 
Dirk has been adopted by a noble.

00:14:52.190 --> 00:14:52.830
What?

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:57.450
It happened yesterday.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:02.030
When Fran and I returned 
from our lunch break

00:15:02.030 --> 00:15:04.690
Delia and Dirk were nowhere to be found.

00:15:04.690 --> 00:15:09.000
Soon after, Wilma told us 
that Delia had taken Dirk.

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:13.480
We had the head priest ask the 
high priest what had happened

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:15.720
and we found out about the adoption.

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:20.970
But doesn't an adoption with a noble 
need to be cleared by the lord first?

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:24.380
Apparently not when it involves 
a noble from another domain.

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:25.980
Really?!

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:28.740
The head priest seemed concerned 
about this matter, too.

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:32.500
What is going to happen to Delia?

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:33.480
Lady Main,

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:35.690
please let go of Delia.

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:37.060
Huh?

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:40.830
She acts on her own without 
permission from her master

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.200
and brings you misfortune.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:45.860
She should not be allowed to 
continue as your attendant.

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:51.430
She should be telling you when 
she goes to see the high priest.

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:59.360
Fran, please summon Delia for me.

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:02.000
As you wish.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:06.890
<i>But the last thing she wanted 
was to be torn apart from Dirk.</i>

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:08.130
<i>Why would she do this?</i>

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:19.320
When I told the high priest 
that the head priest

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:22.570
was looking for someone to adopt 
Dirk and couldn't find anyone...

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:27.320
Oh? The head priest was looking 
for someone to adopt the boy?

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:33.480
But the head priest couldn't find 
anyone, so I'm still looking after him.

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:36.420
He gets these bumps when he starts crying.

00:16:39.110 --> 00:16:41.220
I'm just so worried.

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:45.820
And you should be. I'll go ahead 
and take care of this for you.

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:46.980
Huh?

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:49.860
Leave this to me.

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:54.290
And then the high priest 
found someone immediately!

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:55.530
Isn't that amazing?!

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:57.840
Are you okay with this, Delia?

00:16:57.840 --> 00:17:00.990
Wouldn't this mean you'll be away from Dirk?

00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:06.750
The high priest said that Dirk could stay 
by his side until he comes of age!

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:12.830
Until then, Dirk and I get to stay in 
a room the high priest prepared for us!

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:16.130
There's something very wrong with this.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:20.590
If they're after Dirk's mana, what's the 
point of having the high priest raise him?

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:24.990
Why did this noble agree to adopt Dirk?

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:26.600
Pardon me...

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:29.930
But may I be excused now?

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:32.980
Dirk's new father will be here soon.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:40.200
In that case, I will dismiss 
you as my attendant, Delia.

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:44.010
I'm sure taking care of Dirk will 
be difficult, but do your best.

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:47.010
I will. Please excuse me.

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:56.080
The high priest asked me 
to give you a headache.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:59.060
Anything but going back to 
the orphanage, please...

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:03.010
I'd rather die!

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:09.150
<i>And I thought things were better now...</i>

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:11.430
Lady Main.

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:15.080
I wonder if Dirk and Delia are all right...

00:18:17.060 --> 00:18:21.820
This is a choice Delia made for herself, 
and now that Dirk is no longer an orphan,

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:25.420
our hands are tied.

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:27.490
You're right.

00:18:30.070 --> 00:18:32.760
More importantly, Lady Main,

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:34.790
please be cautious of the high priest.

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:36.030
What?

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:38.800
When I went to fetch Delia earlier,

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:42.170
the high priest was very 
persistent about seeing you.

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:43.980
The high priest was?

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:46.980
He'd been doing everything he 
could to avoid you until now.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:49.970
This sudden change in him is unsettling.

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:55.690
Also, the high priest was involved 
in the incident at the east gate.

00:18:56.890 --> 00:18:59.570
The one who had sent an invitation 
to the noble from another domain

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:01.670
was apparently the high priest.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:18.830
Main! We've come to get you.

00:19:18.830 --> 00:19:21.420
Tuuli, what brings you here?

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:24.440
Let's go home together. It's been 
dangerous lately, hasn't it?

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:26.780
I'll protect you, Main!

00:19:26.780 --> 00:19:29.180
Me, too! I'll protect you, Lady Main!

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.640
Um...

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:36.810
It's dangerous for me to have 
more of you to protect...

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.690
So, listen, Tuuli.

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:44.610
If something were to happen, 
you'd be in more danger than I am.

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:48.290
If it were just me, 
Sir Damuel could protect me.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:49.960
Fine, I got it.

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:52.470
Mister Otto!

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:54.930
It's been a while.

00:19:54.930 --> 00:19:58.700
Main! You're safe! Thank goodness.

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:01.970
Safe? Did something happen?

00:20:02.490 --> 00:20:05.090
Something happened at the east gate.

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:07.560
Why did you let that carriage through?!

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:09.610
Captain! Calm down!

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:13.550
Why didn't my message get relayed to you?!

00:20:17.060 --> 00:20:20.450
Main... Main's in danger!

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:22.370
They let a carriage through?!

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:24.030
Is it the one from the other day?

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:27.260
Yeah, it's the same noble.

00:20:27.260 --> 00:20:29.320
I'm surprised you know about this.

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:31.830
We're looking for him right now.

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:34.520
You contacted the knights, didn't you?

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:38.310
Huh? Um... I'm not sure...

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:42.960
The captain went to the cathedral 
to make sure Main was okay.

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:44.330
You didn't bump into him?

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:45.840
Rot!

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:51.080
Huh? Wha?!

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:53.680
Wait, are you a noble?!

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:57.560
We'll definitely be safe with 
the knights here, right, Tuuli?

00:20:58.580 --> 00:20:59.320
Huh?

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:00.800
Tuuli?

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:07.550
Apprentice Priestess!

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:11.520
<i>H-Help me...</i>

00:21:13.690 --> 00:21:16.070
Help me!

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:53.930
<b>Next Chapter
The Black Protective Charm</b>

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:56.870
Dad, did you actually tell everyone?

00:22:56.870 --> 00:22:58.020
Of course, I did!

00:22:58.020 --> 00:23:02.020
Before we changed shifts, I went to the east 
gate and talked to the one in charge there.

00:23:02.020 --> 00:23:05.530
Then from the south gate, 
west gate, and north gate,

00:23:02.730 --> 00:23:07.610
<b>South</b>

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:04.730
<b>West</b>

00:23:04.730 --> 00:23:07.610
<b>West      North</b>

00:23:05.530 --> 00:23:10.600
I had all of the ones in charge gather 
and told them all Sir Damuel's message!

00:23:10.600 --> 00:23:13.110
Then why didn't they know?

00:23:13.110 --> 00:23:17.500
According to the gatekeeper, the one 
in charge there never told them.

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:19.170
What?!

00:23:19.170 --> 00:23:24.290
That's why the gatekeeper didn't know to 
check to see if the permit was forged!

00:23:24.290 --> 00:23:26.200
Well, I can't blame them.

00:23:26.200 --> 00:23:29.970
Why the hell didn't they 
tell all the gatekeepers?!

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:32.270
I'm gonna go hit him again!

00:23:32.270 --> 00:23:34.530
Dad, don't!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.970
Illustration by: Hebi-Zou
